    "##### Reusable Bradley–Terry Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "| Function | Purpose |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `average_negative_log_likelihood()` | Evaluates how well a parameter vector explains the observed outcomes. |\n",
    "| `bradley_terry_probability()` | Calculates the probability that one item defeats another. |\n",
    "| `build_complete_comparison_edges()` | Creates a graph containing every possible pair. |\n",
    "| `build_two_disconnected_clusters_edges()` | Creates two groups with no comparisons between them. |\n",
    "| `center_parameters()` | Shifts parameters so their mean is zero. |\n",
    "| `extract_undirected_comparison_edges()` | Extracts observed pairs while ignoring who won. |\n",
    "| `extract_directed_win_edges()` | Extracts directed edges from winner to loser. |\n",
    "| `observed_comparison_graph_is_connected()` | Checks whether the observed pairs connect every item. |\n",
    "| `directed_win_graph_is_strongly_connected()` | Checks whether every item is reachable in both directions through wins. |\n",
    "| `ford_condition_holds()` | Checks the condition required for a finite Bradley–Terry MLE. |\n",
    "| `generate_comparison_data_from_edges()` | Simulates `(winner, loser)` outcomes on specified graph edges. |\n",
    "| `estimate_parameters_with_gradient_descent_trace()` | Estimates parameters while recording NLL and parameter values at every iteration. |\n",
    "| `parameter_recovery_error()` | Calculates centred RMSE between true and estimated parameters. |"
   ]
