    "## Experiment 1: Parameter Identifiability\n",
    "\n",
    "In the Bradley–Terry model, each item \\(i\\) has a parameter theta i. The probability that item \\(i\\) defeats item \\(j\\) is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(i\\succ j)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\exp(\\theta_i)}\n",
    "{\\exp(\\theta_i)+\\exp(\\theta_j)}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{1}\n",
    "{1+\\exp[-(\\theta_i-\\theta_j)]}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The probability depends only on the difference\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\theta_i-\\theta_j.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose the same constant \\(c\\) is added to every parameter. Then\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "(\\theta_i+c)-(\\theta_j+c)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\theta_i-\\theta_j.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(i\\succ j;\\boldsymbol{\\theta})\n",
    "=\n",
    "P(i\\succ j;\\boldsymbol{\\theta}+c\\mathbf{1}).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The data cannot distinguish between these shifted parameter vectors. This is called additive non-identifiability.\n",
    "\n",
    "To select one representative from this family of equivalent solutions, we impose the normalization\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\theta_i=0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The following experiment verifies this invariance numerically."
   ]
  },
